# Metadata for benchmarks/e10_e11_multiseed_chunk7_ab_2026-05-17.tsv
#
# Bench:   jxl-encoder/examples/e10_e11_multiseed_chunk7_ab.rs
# Commit:  chunk-7 working copy (parent: 1760b038 squeeze-on-extras chunk-2)
# Date:    2026-05-17
# Host:    AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (water-cooled), 128 GB RAM, Linux WSL2
# Threads: 8 (LosslessConfig::with_threads(8))
# Samples: 2 paired
# Corpus:  /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/
#          (5 photos: 1025469, 1044329, 1189261, 1279330, 1418519)
#
# Cargo features:
#   std parallel parallel-tree-learning
#
# Invocation:
#   cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
#     --features 'std parallel parallel-tree-learning' \
#     --example e10_e11_multiseed_chunk7_ab
#
# What chunk 7 does:
#   - Adds `multi_seed_early_out_after_probe` helper in modular/tree_learn.rs.
#   - After the first 4 seeds (chunk-3 perturbation slot, MULTI_SEED_EARLY_OUT_PROBE_SEEDS)
#     of the e11 16-seed loop, computes the relative spread of token costs.
#   - If spread < 5% (MULTI_SEED_EARLY_OUT_SPREAD_THRESHOLD), breaks out of
#     the seed loop early — the picker keeps its best-so-far tree.
#   - High-variance images (spread >= 5%) keep running all 16 seeds.
#
# Comparison vs chunk 6 (benchmarks/e10_e11_multiseed_chunk6_ab_2026-05-17.tsv):
#
#   image         | c6_bytes | c7_bytes | dB    | c6_ms_med | c7_ms_med | speedup
#   1025469       |   231127 |   231461 |  +334 |     27384 |      5969 | 4.59x
#   1044329       |   327001 |   327001 |    +0 |     14846 |      6143 | 2.42x
#   1189261       |   302399 |   302399 |    +0 |     18127 |      6234 | 2.91x
#   1279330       |   206214 |   207027 |  +813 |     24723 |      4404 | 5.61x
#   1418519       |   164133 |   164133 |    +0 |     31507 |      7453 | 4.23x
#
#   TOTALS bytes: c6=1,230,874 B → c7=1,232,021 B  (+1147 B, +0.0932%)
#   TOTALS wall:  c6=116,587 ms → c7=30,204 ms     (3.86× speedup at e11 median)
#
# Honest finding from per-seed cost tracing:
#   - 3/5 photos byte-identical with c6 (1044329, 1189261, 1418519)
#   - 2/5 photos regress (1025469: +334B, 1279330: +813B)
#   - The "low chunk-3 spread predicts no further improvement" hypothesis is
#     PARTIALLY FALSE: 1279330 has the lowest chunk-3 spread (0.31%) but
#     seeds 4..15 DO find a 0.69% cost improvement (seed 4 wins).
#     Similarly 1025469 has spread 1.71% but seed 9 wins (0.034% cost).
#   - The 5% threshold is calibrated as a Pareto sweet spot: maximizes
#     wall-clock savings (3.86×) while keeping byte regression to ~0.09%.
#
# Hash-locks:    36/36 byte-identical (tests/hash_lock_features.rs unchanged
#                since e ≤ 9 has tree_learn_seeds = 1 → early-out never enters).
# Unit tests:    12/12 pass (tests::test_early_out_*).
# rd-regression: not re-run (changes only affect e10/e11 lossless paths).
#
# Files changed:
#   jxl-encoder/src/modular/tree_learn.rs   (+helper, +const, +tests)
#   jxl-encoder/src/modular/section.rs      (+early-out wire-up)
#   jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml                  (+[[example]] registration)
#   jxl-encoder/examples/e10_e11_multiseed_chunk7_ab.rs (new)
